Treat an unmapped class as "no metadata" again, so building the implicitly-audited type
set cannot fail the first save after an auditlog global property changes.

openmrs-module-auditlog (master ba96ba5, and the 1.1 release) asks
SessionFactory.getClassMetadata(Class) for arbitrary classes and treats null as "not an
entity". Hibernate 3 returned null; Hibernate 5 (core 2.x) throws MappingException
instead. DAOUtils.getAssociationTypesToAuditInternal() does this for the element type of
every collection property, so the first entity with a value collection (for example a
collection of String) throws "Unknown entity: java.lang.String".

That method runs when AuditLogHelper builds its implicitly-audited type cache: under the
ALL_EXCEPT strategy with a non-empty auditlog.exceptions, the first time an excluded or
unaudited type is saved after the cache was reset, which every change to auditlog.* does.
The exception escapes onSave() and fails that save. The cache is left half-built and
non-null, so no later save fails, which is why only one save per boot was lost.

On a LiberiaEMR clean install that save was the OCL importer's startImport() for the FIRST
dictionary zip, in a daemon thread whose exception openmrs-core's
Daemon.runInDaemonThreadAndWait() swallows. Initializer logged only "OCL import did not
start successfully", the whole zip was skipped (678 concepts of LIB/mch in CI), and every
drug, concept set, program and report set that referenced them was rejected.

The fix makes DAOUtils.getClassMetadata() return null on MappingException, as every caller
assumes, and routes the two direct calls through it. It also stops casting a OneToOneType
to CollectionType, which would throw ClassCastException for any entity with a one-to-one
property once the cache build got that far.

Applied by distribution/backend/Dockerfile (stage 2b). Tracked in
packages/modify-pr/.patches/0004-openmrs-module-auditlog-unmapped-class-metadata.md.

